  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aEYXl",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3803138942,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 227,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3803138942",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The service enforces scheme/host/DNS/private-address policy, but it never checks that `request.DocumentId` (and optionally `BookingId`) is actually consistent with `request.DocumentUrl` (e.g., that the URL path/filename corresponds to the validated document id). This weakens the “validated context” contract and can allow downloading a different resource on an allowlisted host than the caller intended. Consider adding a strict consistency check (e.g., ensure the last path segment matches `{DocumentId}.pdf` or otherwise deterministically binds the URL to the provided document id; also consider binding booking id if it appears in the path) and reject mismatches as a controlled validation/policy failure.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Valid. The documented download contract requires document-id/document-url consistency, but the service previously trusted the caller-provided ID independently of the allowlisted URL. Already resolved at the reviewed HEAD (cb8620054b): RetrieveDocument requires the decoded final path segment to equal {DocumentId}.pdf before DNS resolution or download and maps mismatches to the existing controlled bad-request path; BookingControllerTests.RetrieveDocument_Returns_BadRequest_When_DocumentId_Does_Not_Match_Url provides regression coverage."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aEbH7",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3803155421,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 227,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3803155421",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The service accepts both `DocumentId` and `DocumentUrl` but never verifies they are consistent (e.g., that the URL path/filename corresponds to `DocumentId`, and optionally `BookingId`). This can lead to returning bytes for one document while labeling it as another `DocumentId` (and it weakens the documented 'Verify ID/URL consistency' policy). Add an explicit consistency check before fetching (e.g., compare `Path.GetFileName(documentUri.AbsolutePath)` / expected suffix, and reject mismatches with a controlled failure).",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Valid duplicate of thread PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aEYXl. Already resolved at the reviewed HEAD (cb8620054b): RetrieveDocument requires the decoded final path segment to equal {DocumentId}.pdf before DNS resolution or download and maps mismatches to the existing controlled bad-request path; BookingControllerTests.RetrieveDocument_Returns_BadRequest_When_DocumentId_Does_Not_Match_Url provides regression coverage."
    },
